NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001638 "=item * B<verbose> => I<bool>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001639 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001640 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001641 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001642 "=item * B<version> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001643 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001644 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001645 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001646 "=item * B<yaml> => I<bool>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001647 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001648 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001649 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001650 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001651 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001652 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001653 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001654 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001655 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001656 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001657 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001658 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001659 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001660 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001661 ""
