NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001664 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001665 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001666 "=head2 completion"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001667 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001668 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001669 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001670 " completion(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001671 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001672 "Do nothing, return args."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001673 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001674 "This function is used to test argument completion."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001675 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001676 "This function is not exported."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001677 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001678 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001679 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001680 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001681 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001682 "=item * B<a1> => I<array[str]>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001683 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001684 "Array of strings, where the string has \"in\" schema clause."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001685 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001686 "Completion library can perhaps complete from the C<in> value and remember"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001687 "completed items when command-line option is repeated, e.g. in:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001688 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001689 " --a1 <tab>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001690 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001691 "it will complete from any C<in> value, but in:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001692 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001693 " --a1 apple --a1 <tab>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001694 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001695 "it can exclude C<apple> from the completion candidate."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001696 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001697 "Currently the completion library L<Perinci::Sub::Complete> does not do this"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001698 "though. Perhaps there can be an option to toggle this behavior."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001699 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001700 "=item * B<a2> => I<array[str]>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001701 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001702 "Array with element_completion routine that generate random letter."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001703 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001704 "=item * B<a3> => I<array[str]>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001705 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001706 "Array with element_completion routine that dies."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001707 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001708 "See also C<s3>."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001709 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001710 "=item * B<arg0> => I<any>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001711 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001712 "Argument without any schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001713 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001714 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001715 "=item * B<f0> => I<float>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001716 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001717 "Float with just \"float\" schema defined."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001718 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001719 "=item * B<f1> => I<float>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001720 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001721 "Float with xminE<sol>xmax on the schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001722 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001723 "A completion library can attempt to provide some possible and incremental"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001724 "completion (e.g. if word is currently at one decimal digit like 1.2, it can"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001725 "provide completion of 1.20 .. 1.29)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001726 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001727 "=item * B<h1> => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001728 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001729 "Hash with \"keys\" and \"allowed_keys\" schema clauses and \"element_completion\" property."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001730 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001731 "=item * B<h2> => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001732 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001733 "Hash with \"element_completion\" as well as \"index_completion\" properties."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001734 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001735 "=item * B<i0> => I<int>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001736 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001737 "Integer with just \"int\" schema defined."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001738 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001739 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001740 "=item * B<i1> => I<int>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001741 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001742 "Integer with minE<sol>xmax on the schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001743 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001744 "A completion library (like L<Perinci::Sub::Complete>) can generate a list of"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001745 "completion from the low end to the high end of the range, as long as it is not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001746 "too long."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001747 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001748 "=item * B<i2> => I<int>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001749 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001750 "Integer with large range minE<sol>max on the schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001751 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001752 "Unlike in C<i1>, a completion library probably won't generate a number sequence"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001753 "for this argument because they are considered too long (1000+ items)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001754 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001755 "=item * B<s1> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001756 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001757 "String with possible values in \"in\" schema clause."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001758 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001759 "=item * B<s1b> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001760 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001761 "String with possible values in \"in\" schema clause, contains special characters."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001762 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001763 "This argument is intended to test how special characters are escaped."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001764 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001765 "=item * B<s1c> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001766 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001767 "String with examples in schema."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001768 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001769 "=item * B<s1d> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001770 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001771 "String with examples in argument spec."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001772 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001773 "=item * B<s2> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001774 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001775 "String with completion routine that generate random letter."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001776 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001777 "=item * B<s3> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001778 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001779 "String with completion routine that dies."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001780 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001781 "Completion should not display error (except perhaps under debugging). It should"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001782 "just provide no completion."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001783 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001784 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001785 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001786 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001787 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001788 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001789 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001790 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001791 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001792 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001793 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001794 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001795 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001796 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001797 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001798 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00001799 ""
