NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002148 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002149 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002150 " merge_hash(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002151 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002152 "Merge two hashes."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002153 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002154 "This function can be used to test passing nonscalar (hash) arguments."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002155 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002156 "This function also tests the C<x.perinci.sub.wrapper.disable_validate_args>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002157 "attribute so that L<Perinci::Sub::Wrapper> does not generate argument"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002158 "validation code in the wrapper. Note that by adding C<# VALIDATE_ARG> in the"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002159 "source code, the L<Dist::Zilla::Plugin::Rinci::Wrap> plugin already generates"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002160 "and embeds argument validation code in the source code, so duplication is not"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002161 "desired, thus the attribute."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002162 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002163 "This function is not exported."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002164 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002165 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002166 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002167 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002168 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002169 "=item * B<h1>* => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002170 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002171 "First hash (left-hand side)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002172 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002173 "=item * B<h2>* => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002174 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002175 "First hash (right-hand side)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002176 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002177 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002178 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002179 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002180 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002181 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002182 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002183 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002184 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002185 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002186 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002187 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002188 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002189 "Return value:  (hash)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002190 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002191 ""
