NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002513 "=head2 undescribed_args"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002514 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002515 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002516 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002517 " undescribed_args(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002518 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002519 "This function has several undescribed args."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002520 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002521 "Originally added to see how peri-func-usage or L<Perinci::To::Text> will"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002522 "display the usage or documentation for this function."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002523 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002524 "This function is not exported."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002525 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002526 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002527 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002528 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002529 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002530 "=item * B<arg1> => I<any>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002531 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002532 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002533 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002534 "=item * B<arg2> => I<any>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002535 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002536 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002537 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002538 "=item * B<arg3> => I<any>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002539 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002540 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002541 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002542 "=item * B<arg4> => I<any>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002543 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002544 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002545 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002546 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002547 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002548 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002549 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002550 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002551 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002552 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002553 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002554 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002555 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002556 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002557 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002558 "Return value:  (any)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002559 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002560 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002561 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002562 "=head2 validate_args"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002563 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002564 "Usage:"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002565 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002566 " validate_args(%args) -> [$status_code, $reason, $payload, \\%result_meta]"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002567 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002568 "Does nothing, only here to test # VALIDATE_ARGS."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002569 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002570 "This function is not exported."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002571 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002572 "Arguments ('*' denotes required arguments):"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002573 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002574 "=over 4"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002575 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002576 "=item * B<a> => I<int>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002577 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002578 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002579 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002580 "=item * B<b> => I<str>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002581 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002582 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002583 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002584 "=item * B<h1> => I<hash>"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002585 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002586 "(No description)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002587 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002588 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002589 "=back"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002590 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002591 "Returns an enveloped result (an array)."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002592 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002593 "First element ($status_code) is an integer containing HTTP-like status code"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002594 "(200 means OK, 4xx caller error, 5xx function error). Second element"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002595 "($reason) is a string containing error message, or something like \"OK\" if status is"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002596 "200. Third element ($payload) is the actual result, but usually not present when enveloped result is an error response ($status_code is not 2xx). Fourth"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002597 "element (%result_meta) is called result metadata and is optional, a hash"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002598 "that contains extra information, much like how HTTP response headers provide additional metadata."
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002599 ""
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002600 "Return value:  (str)"
NSQ_SOURCE_LINE 00002601 ""
